  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>(i) Ionic mobilities decreases with increase in temperature due to increase in random motion and hence decrease in relaxation time so derease in drift speed.</p><p>(i)&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaCl</mi></math>&nbsp;is completely soluble salt while&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>BaSO</mi><mn>4</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is sparingly soluble salt so&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>.</p><p>(ii) On increasse in temperature conductance increase.</p>",
